# MRIDHAOS

**MRIDHAOS** is a lightweight, USB-bootable Linux operating system designed for hobbyists, programmers, and privacy-focused users. It boots into a fast, distraction-free terminal with full console mouse support (`gpm`), classic **BASIC** programming, and on-demand graphical applications (**Firefox**, **Steam**, **LibreOffice**, and **File Managers**) that launch only when you call them—closing straight back to the terminal when finished.

---

## Download

* **Download ISO:** [MRIDHAOS.iso (v1.0 - 64-bit x86_64)](https://github.com<YOUR-USERNAME>/<YOUR-REPO>/releases/latest)
* **Supported Hardware:**
  * Any 64-bit (`x86_64` / `amd64`) Intel or AMD laptop or desktop (UEFI or Legacy BIOS).
  * Includes universal X11 display drivers (Intel, AMD, NVIDIA/Nouveau, VESA) and `linux-firmware` for Wi-Fi/Bluetooth.
  * **Minimum Specs:** 2 GB RAM (4 GB+ recommended for Firefox and Steam), 8 GB+ USB flash drive (16 GB–32 GB+ recommended for encrypted persistence).
  * **Important:** Disable **Secure Boot** in your PC's BIOS/UEFI before booting from USB. Does not support ARM devices (Apple M1/M2/M3/M4 or Raspberry Pi).

---

## Built-In Commands

MRIDHAOS boots into a pure text console with mouse cursor support. Run any command below on demand:

| Command | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `basic` | Launch the **Bywater BASIC** interpreter (`~/scripts`) |
| `fm` | Open **Midnight Commander** (terminal file manager with mouse support) |
| `files` | Launch **PCManFM** graphical file manager |
| `web` | Launch graphical **Firefox** browser |
| `game` | Launch graphical **Steam** client |
| `office` | Launch **LibreOffice** suite hub |
| `write [file.docx]` | Launch **LibreOffice Writer** (Word Processor) |
| `calc [file.xlsx]` | Launch **LibreOffice Calc** (Spreadsheets) |
| `slides [file.pptx]` | Launch **LibreOffice Impress** (Presentations) |
| `pdf <file.pdf>` | Open **Atril** PDF viewer |
| `nmcli dev wifi connect "<SSID>" password "<PASS>"` | Connect to a Wi-Fi network |
| `sudo poweroff` | Safely shut down and lock encrypted storage |

---

## Installation: Flashing to USB & Setting Up LUKS2 Encryption

### 1. Flash `MRIDHAOS.iso` to Your USB Drive
Replace `/dev/sdX` with your actual USB drive (check with `lsblk` first—do **not** pick your internal hard drive):

```bash
sudo umount /dev/sdX* 2>/dev/null
sudo dd if=MRIDHAOS.iso of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress && sync
```

### 2. Create an Encrypted Persistent Storage Partition (LUKS2)
1. **Create a new partition in the remaining free space on your USB stick:**
   ```bash
   echo -e "n\np\n\n\n\nw" | sudo fdisk /dev/sdX
   sudo partprobe /dev/sdX
   lsblk /dev/sdX
   ```
   *(Note the name of the new partition at the bottom, e.g., `/dev/sdX5` or `/dev/sdX3`.)*

2. **Encrypt the partition with LUKS2 (AES-256-XTS + Argon2id):**
   *(Type `YES` in uppercase when prompted, then enter your chosen passphrase twice.)*
   ```bash
   sudo cryptsetup luksFormat --type luks2 \
       --cipher aes-xts-plain64 --key-size 512 \
       --hash sha512 --pbkdf argon2id \
       /dev/sdX5
   ```

3. **Format the unlocked partition as `persistence`:**
   ```bash
   sudo cryptsetup open /dev/sdX5 mridha_crypt
   sudo mkfs.ext4 -L persistence /dev/mapper/mridha_crypt
   sudo mount /dev/mapper/mridha_crypt /mnt
   echo "/ union" | sudo tee /mnt/persistence.conf
   sudo umount /mnt
   sudo cryptsetup close mridha_crypt
   sync
   ```

When you boot from the USB drive, MRIDHAOS will pause and ask for your LUKS passphrase before unlocking your personal files, browser profile, Steam library, and BASIC scripts.

---

## How to Change or Add a New Encryption Password

LUKS2 supports up to **8 independent key slots** on the same encrypted partition (`/dev/sdX5`).

### Option A: Change Your Current Encryption Password
Replace `/dev/sdX5` with your encrypted USB partition:
```bash
sudo cryptsetup luksChangeKey /dev/sdX5
```
1. Enter your **current passphrase**.
2. Enter your **new passphrase** twice.

### Option B: Add a Second (Backup Recovery) Password
Keep your daily password in Slot 0 and add a separate recovery passphrase in Slot 1:
```bash
sudo cryptsetup luksAddKey /dev/sdX5
```
1. Enter your **existing passphrase**.
2. Enter the **new backup passphrase** twice.

### Option C: Remove an Old Password
```bash
sudo cryptsetup luksRemoveKey /dev/sdX5
```
*(Enter the passphrase you want to delete—make sure at least one valid passphrase remains.)*
### Connecting to Wi-Fi

Because MRIDHAOS runs in a pure terminal without a desktop keyring, connect to Wi-Fi using:

```bash
nmcli connection add type wifi con-name "mywifi" ifname "*" ssid "YOUR_WIFI_NAME" \
    wifi-sec.key-mgmt wpa-psk \
    wifi-sec.psk-flags 0 \
    wifi-sec.psk "YOUR_PASSWORD"
nmcli connection up "mywifi"
```

| `nmtui` | Open interactive terminal menu to scan and connect to any Wi-Fi network |

# MRIDHAOS

**MRIDHAOS** is a lightweight, USB-bootable and dual-bootable Linux operating system designed for hobbyists, programmers, and privacy-focused users. It boots into a fast, distraction-free terminal with full console mouse support (`gpm`), classic **BASIC** programming, and on-demand graphical applications (**Firefox**, **Steam**, **LibreOffice**, and **File Managers**) that launch only when you call them—closing straight back to the terminal when finished.

---

## Download

* **Download ISO (Zipped):** [MRIDHAOS-v1.0.zip (64-bit x86_64)](https://github.com)
* **Supported Hardware:**
  * Any 64-bit (`x86_64` / `amd64`) Intel or AMD laptop or desktop (UEFI or Legacy BIOS).
  * Includes universal X11 display drivers (Intel, AMD, NVIDIA/Nouveau, VESA) and `linux-firmware` for Wi-Fi/Bluetooth.
  * **Minimum Specs:** 2 GB RAM (4 GB+ recommended for Firefox and Steam), 8 GB+ USB flash drive (16 GB–32 GB+ recommended for encrypted persistence).
  * **Important:** Disable **Secure Boot** in your PC's BIOS/UEFI before booting from USB. Does not support ARM devices (Apple M1/M2/M3/M4 or Raspberry Pi).

---

## Built-In Commands

MRIDHAOS boots into a pure text console with mouse cursor support. Run any command below on demand:

| Command | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `basic` | Launch the **Bywater BASIC** interpreter (`~/scripts`) |
| `fm` | Open **Midnight Commander** (terminal file manager with mouse support) |
| `files` | Launch **PCManFM** graphical file manager |
| `web` | Launch graphical **Firefox** browser |
| `game` | Launch graphical **Steam** client |
| `office` | Launch **LibreOffice** suite hub |
| `write [file.docx]` | Launch **LibreOffice Writer** (Word Processor) |
